=== Direct left recursion ===
  Left-recursive arithmetic          LEFT-RECURSIVE: ['E', 'T']
                                     -> recursive descent will loop forever
  Right-recursive arithmetic         no direct left recursion
  Balanced parentheses               no direct left recursion
  Statement list (separator)         LEFT-RECURSIVE: ['L']
                                     -> recursive descent will loop forever

=== The one the detector MISSES ===
  Indirect: A -> B c, B -> A d       no direct left recursion
  ...and yet parse_A() calls parse_B(), which calls parse_A().
  Neither rule begins with ITSELF, so the direct check cannot see it.

=== Watch the loop, with a depth guard so we survive it ===
    depth 12 reached: E -> E -> E -> E -> E -> E -> E -> E ...
  grammar_lr   starting at E: LOOPED
  grammar_rr   starting at E: consumed a terminal, fine
    depth 12 reached: A -> B -> A -> B -> A -> B -> A -> B ...
  indirect     starting at A: LOOPED
